class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        // Arrays.sort(nums);

        int n = nums.length;
        int low = 0;
        int mid = 0;
        int high = n-1;
        while(mid<=high){
            // repositioning 0
            if(nums[mid]==0){
                int temp = nums[low];
                nums[low] = nums[mid];
                nums[mid] = temp;
                low++;
                mid++;
            }
            //repositioning 1
            else if(nums[mid]==1){
                mid++;
            }
            // repositioning 2
            else if(nums[mid]==2){
                int temp = nums[mid];
                nums[mid]=nums[high];
                nums[high]=temp;
                high--;
            }
        }
    }
}

Implemented the Dutch National Flag algorithm to sort an array of colors represented by 0s, 1s, and 2s in a single pass.

Problem Link : https://leetcode.com/problems/sort-colors/
